claim.claim-text:
a coupling structure adapted to be coupled to the pen type syringe body;
a post configured to accommodate the needle so that a proximal end portion of the needle extends into the coupling structure and a distal end portion of the needle is exposed from a surface of the needle hub/the post;
a needle hole provided in the needle hub/the post in which a body of the needle is accommodated; and
an adhesive storage portion configured to store an adhesive used to allow the needle and the needle hub to adhere to each other in the post, and
a plurality of ribs radially formed around the post and configured to increase a contact area with user's skin while injection is performed.

a post extending in a direction in which the needle extends and configured to accommodate the needle to allow a distal end portion of the needle to be exposed from a surface of the needle hub;
a needle hole in which a body of the needle is inserted;
an adhesive storage portion configured to store an adhesive used to allow the needle and the needle hub to adhere to each other in the post; and
a leaking adhesive storage portion formed on one end of the needle hole and having a surface area increased in comparison to a surface area of the needle hole.
